        "original_id": "9bd8f154-c0cc-5311-be53-6c7ea3c65af5",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Igor Dmitriev, Rosencrantz, Guildenstern, Hamlet, King Claudius, Grigori Kozintsev, Yan Frid, Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov\n- Works: Hamlet, The Green Carriage\n- Roles: Film actor, theater actor, aristocratic characters\n- Topics: Shakespeare characters, Soviet historical drama film\n\nFacts:\n- Igor Borisovich Dmitriev was born on May 29, 1927, and died on January 26, 2008.\n- Igor Dmitriev was a Russian film and theater actor who specialized in playing aristocratic characters in costume productions.\n- Rosencrantz is a childhood friend of Hamlet.\n- Guildenstern is a childhood friend of Hamlet.\n- Rosencrantz and Guildenstern were summoned by King Claudius to distract Hamlet from his apparent madness and, if possible, discover its cause.\n- In Grigori Kozintsev's Hamlet, Igor Dmitriev played Rosencrantz.\n- The Green Carriage is a 1967 Soviet historical drama film directed by Yan Frid.\n- The Green Carriage starred Natalya Tenyakova, Vladimir Chestnokov, and Igor Dmitriev.",
